30,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems our history is bleak. The eastern avenue trees died due to poor aftercare, though the overflow basin is still solid.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The ground is a risk. Firms are flagging clay subsoil and slippage. We should avoid heavy earth-moving if possible.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The funding is restrictive! The habitat fund only pays for planting and water, not buildings. Plus, greenery costs triple to maintain.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,Our staff is depleted. We've gone from eighteen posts to seven. We are relying heavily on bought-in services for specialist care.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"People are using the park as a thoroughfare to the tram, sticking to firm ground. Also, drainage issues are doubling.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, if the soil is that unstable, any plan requiring massive excavation is a recipe for disaster.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"Precisely. Shallow work is fine, but deep digging will lead to the ""drifting"" dates I fear.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, if we have so few staff, we absolutely cannot afford a high-maintenance landscape. The ledger proves it's too expensive.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. However, we do have volunteer groups for habitat and sports. That's a potential resource we can leverage.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Mio, the heat readings were high last August. We need shade or water, but it must be something that doesn't clog the drains.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"The fact that the overflow basin survived while the pavement failed suggests that ""natural"" water management is more durable here.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"But we must be careful. If we go too ""natural"" with heavy planting, we hit that clay slippage risk.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,And the habitat fund only pays for that specific type of work. We can't afford to build a plaza if the fund won't cover it.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,We have to balance the fund's requirements with the fact that we have almost no one to mow a lawn or prune trees.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"If people are just crossing the site to the tram, we shouldn't put obstacles in their way.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It sounds like we need something durable, low-excavation, and potentially funded by the habitat grant.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"And something that doesn't require the whole site to be closed at once, given the depot notes.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,Low maintenance is non-negotiable. I won't support a plan that bankrupts the upkeep budget.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,Let's see the candidates and see which one fits these harsh realities.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,Agreed. Let's look at the options.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
