59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"We have Market Plaza, Woodland Walk, Wetland Restoration, and Sports Terraces. The Plaza seems too ""hard"" given the previous pavement failures.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,The Woodland Walk might be too much earth-moving for the clay. Sports Terraces also sound like a construction nightmare.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mio,,"The Wetland Restoration fits the habitat fund perfectly. It covers planting and water management, which is all the fund pays for.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Wetland care is specialist, but we have volunteers who already work on habitat tasks upriver. They could help.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Wetland Restoration also addresses the drainage callouts and the August heat. It works with the water, not against it.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, does it interfere with the tram commuters? Boardwalks could keep people on firm ground while preserving the margins.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,It's likely shallow work compared to building courts or a massive plaza. It's the safest bet for the soil.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mio,,And it avoids the high cost of hard-surfacing maintenance that I saw in the ledgers.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"The Sports Terraces would require too much stewarding. We don't have the staff for that, even with the casual pool.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,The Market Plaza would just be a heat sink in August. The wetlands provide actual cooling.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I'm convinced. The durability of the previous overflow basin proves that water-based infrastructure is our strongest suit.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. It minimizes the risk of slippage and avoids the construction delays associated with heavy building.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mio,,It's the only one that aligns with the regional habitat fund's strict terms. It's the only fiscally responsible choice.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"With the habitat volunteers already in place, it's the most sustainable option for our limited staff.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,It solves the drainage problem and respects the way the land behaves. I vote for Wetland Restoration.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. Wetland Restoration it is.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mio,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
